# v32tools manifest -- the single source of truth for the Makefile AND the CMake
# infrastructure. One tool per line, in BUILD ORDER (the order the tools are
# built, cleaned, installed, ...). Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# Columns are separated by whitespace; the last column (description) runs to the
# end of the line.
#
#   name      directory name under tools/ (also the target name: `make v32as`)
#   backends  comma list of native build systems the tool offers: make, cmake
#   hostdeps  comma list of host programs needed to BUILD the tool ('-' = none).
#             'cc' means any C compiler (cc, gcc or clang). flex is special: if
#             it is missing, v32tools can build the vendored deps/flex-*.tar.gz.
#   url       git URL used by `make bootstrap` / scripts/add-tool.sh
#   description
#
# Add a tool: see docs/ADDING-A-TOOL.md  (or: scripts/add-tool.sh NAME URL ...)
#
# name    backends    hostdeps         url                                       description
v32as     make        cc,flex,bison    https://github.com/wedge1020/v32as.git    Vircon32 assembler (v32as) and linker (v32asld)
v32opt    make,cmake  cc               https://github.com/wedge1020/v32opt.git   Assembly optimizer
v32sim    make        cc,flex,bison    https://github.com/wedge1020/v32sim.git   Text-based debugger, profiler and simulator (needs GNU readline)
v32cc     make        cc,flex,bison    https://github.com/wedge1020/v32cc.git    C compiler (v32cc) and C library
v32lua    make,cmake  cc,flex,bison    https://github.com/wedge1020/v32lua.git   Lua-subset to Vircon32 assembly translator
v32cxx    make,cmake  cc,flex,bison    https://github.com/wedge1020/v32cxx.git   C++ subset to C transpiler (v32c++ / v32c)
